        <strong>Figure 6.1: Dual-Axis Utilization Collapse &amp; Host-Issue Scaling Sensitivity.</strong> As algorithms transition from compute-bound matrix multiplies to element-wise reduction loops, the host scalar core becomes the bottleneck, causing vector utilization to collapse from 98.4% to 23.0%. Autonomous DAE stream registers (SSR) bypass the host issue tube entirely, restoring 95%+ compute saturation.
      </p>
