      <div class="dossier-body">
        <p>CV32E40P is a silicon-proven, 4-stage in-order RISC-V core featuring the PULP XpulpV2 instruction set extension. Rather than implementing a dedicated vector register file, CV32E40P slices standard 32-bit general-purpose registers into 2&times;16-bit or 4&times;8-bit sub-words. Its dual-multiply accumulator executes dot products (<code>pv.dotsp.b</code>) in a single cycle.</p>

        <!-- RTL Configuration Parameters Table -->
        <h4 style="font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 800; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #151b20;">&bull; Key RTL Configuration Parameters</h4>
        <div class="table-wrap" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          <table class="data-table" style="font-size: 0.8rem;">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Default</th><th>Silicon Impact</th><th>Description</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>PULP_XPULP</code></td><td><code>1</code></td><td>DSP Instruction Support</td><td>Enables packed-SIMD, hardware loops, and bit manipulation.</td></tr><tr><td><code>PULP_CLUSTER</code></td><td><code>0</code></td><td>Cluster Binding</td><td>Configures core for standalone or multi-core cluster operation.</td></tr><tr><td><code>FPU</code></td><td><code>1</code></td><td>Hardware FPU</td><td>Instantiates IEEE-754 single-precision floating-point unit.</td></tr><tr><td><code>ZFINX</code></td><td><code>0</code></td><td>Float Register File</td><td>0: Dedicated FPRs; 1: Shares integer register file.</td></tr><tr><td><code>NUM_MHPMCOUNTERS</code></td><td><code>1</code></td><td>Performance Monitors</td><td>Number of hardware performance counters instantiated.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <!-- Microarchitectural Deep-Dive -->
        <div class="dossier-deep-dive" style="background: #f8fafc; border-left: 3px solid #3b82f6; padding: 0.85rem 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;">
          <h4 style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 900; color: #1e3a8a; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">Microarchitectural Deep-Dive:</h4>
          <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.5; color: #334155; margin: 0;">CV32E40P's packed SIMD unit operates directly on <code>rs1</code> and <code>rs2</code> GPRs. For 8-bit dot products, the core reads two 32-bit registers, performs four concurrent 8&times;8 multiplications, sums the results through a two-level adder tree, and adds the sum to an accumulator in a single clock cycle without extra vector state.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Verified Benchmarks Table -->
