            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>NLanes</code></td><td><code>4</code></td><td>Datapath Slices</td><td>Number of parallel vector execution lanes.</td></tr><tr><td><code>VRFSize</code></td><td><code>256 KB</code></td><td>VRF Storage</td><td>Total vector register file capacity.</td></tr><tr><td><code>PredicateRegs</code></td><td><code>16</code></td><td>Predication</td><td>Number of predicate registers for conditional execution.</td></tr><tr><td><code>QueueDepth</code></td><td><code>16</code></td><td>Decoupling Queue</td><td>Capacity of operand buffering FIFOs.</td></tr><tr><td><code>HostInterface</code></td><td><code>RoCC</code></td><td>Host Coupling</td><td>Rocket Custom Coprocessor command interface.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <!-- Microarchitectural Deep-Dive -->
        <div class="dossier-deep-dive" style="background: #f8fafc; border-left: 3px solid #3b82f6; padding: 0.85rem 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;">
          <h4 style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 900; color: #1e3a8a; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">Microarchitectural Deep-Dive:</h4>
          <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.5; color: #334155; margin: 0;">Hwacha completely separates vector address generation from arithmetic. The vector memory unit generates burst requests and loads operands directly into decoupled FIFOs. The arithmetic lanes execute autonomously from these queues, completely decoupled from host CPU instruction issue latency.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Verified Benchmarks Table -->
