        <h3 class="dossier-title">Integrated Matrix Extension &bull; 2D Tile Tensor Coprocessor (IME / SME)</h3>
        <span class="dossier-sub">RISC-V Non-ISA Community &bull; Apache-2.0 &bull; SystemVerilog</span>
      </div>

      <!-- Specs Stack -->
      <div class="dossier-specs-grid">
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">ISA:</span><span class="s-v"><code>RISC-V Matrix Extension (SME / IME)</code></span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Lanes:</span><span class="s-v">16 Parallel Lanes &bull; 2D Outer-Product Mesh</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Vector Length:</span><span class="s-v">8&times;8 Matrix Tile Registers</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">VRF Architecture:</span><span class="s-v">1D VRF (512b) + 2D Accumulator Tiles (ZA)</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Host / Bus Interface:</span><span class="s-v">AXI4 / TileLink 256-bit Bus</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Silicon Footprint:</span><span class="s-v"><strong>~310 kGE (12nm)</strong></span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Peak Frequency:</span><span class="s-v">1.2 GHz (GF 12LP)</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Verification Status:</span><span class="s-v">SCORE Literature Reported (ISCA 2023 / DATE 2024)</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="dossier-body">
        <p>The Integrated Matrix Extension (IME) bridges 1D vector computing and 2D spatial systolic arrays. By introducing 2D accumulator tile registers (ZA) and outer-product instructions (<code>mopa</code>), IME executes matrix multiplication directly on 2D register state with spatial data reuse, achieving 128 Ops/cycle while preserving general-purpose vector flexibility.</p>

        <!-- RTL Configuration Parameters Table -->
        <h4 style="font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 800; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #151b20;">&bull; Key RTL Configuration Parameters</h4>
        <div class="table-wrap" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          <table class="data-table" style="font-size: 0.8rem;">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Default</th><th>Silicon Impact</th><th>Description</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>TileRows</code></td><td><code>8</code></td><td>Tile Dimensions</td><td>Number of rows per 2D accumulator tile.</td></tr><tr><td><code>TileCols</code></td><td><code>8</code></td><td>Tile Dimensions</td><td>Number of columns per 2D accumulator tile.</td></tr><tr><td><code>AccBits</code></td><td><code>32</code></td><td>Accumulator Depth</td><td>Bit-width of each tile accumulator element (INT32 / FP32).</td></tr><tr><td><code>VectorLanes</code></td><td><code>16</code></td><td>Input Lanes</td><td>Number of 1D vector lanes feeding outer-product unit.</td></tr><tr><td><code>TransposeUnits</code></td><td><code>2</code></td><td>In-Flight Transpose</td><td>Dedicated hardware units for zero-cycle matrix rotation.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <!-- Microarchitectural Deep-Dive -->
        <div class="dossier-deep-dive" style="background: #f8fafc; border-left: 3px solid #3b82f6; padding: 0.85rem 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;">
          <h4 style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 900; color: #1e3a8a; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">Microarchitectural Deep-Dive:</h4>
          <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.5; color: #334155; margin: 0;">IME executes outer products by broadcasting elements of vector operand A horizontally while streaming vector operand B vertically. The resulting 16&times;8 partial matrix slice accumulates directly into the local 2D tile register file (ZA) without generating inter-bank register file conflicts.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Verified Benchmarks Table -->
        <h4 style="font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 800; margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #151b20;">&bull; Cycle-Accurate Verified Benchmark Results</h4>
