      <div class="dossier-body">
        <p>Vortex is an open-source RISC-V GPGPU coprocessor executing OpenCL 1.2 and CUDA kernels via fine-grained Single Instruction Multiple Threads (SIMT). Featuring dynamic warp schedulers, hardware branch divergence stacks, and 16-lane vector execution units, Vortex delivers high thread-level parallelism and memory latency tolerance.</p>

        <!-- RTL Configuration Parameters Table -->
        <h4 style="font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 800; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #151b20;">&bull; Key RTL Configuration Parameters</h4>
        <div class="table-wrap" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          <table class="data-table" style="font-size: 0.8rem;">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Default</th><th>Silicon Impact</th><th>Description</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>NUM_CORES</code></td><td><code>4</code></td><td>Multi-Core Scaling</td><td>Number of clustered SIMT GPGPU cores.</td></tr><tr><td><code>NUM_WARPS</code></td><td><code>4</code></td><td>Warp Scheduling</td><td>Number of concurrent thread warps per core.</td></tr><tr><td><code>NUM_THREADS</code></td><td><code>16</code></td><td>Warp Width</td><td>Number of parallel execution threads per warp.</td></tr><tr><td><code>L1_LINE_SIZE</code></td><td><code>64</code></td><td>Cache Line Width</td><td>Byte width of L1 instruction and data cache lines.</td></tr><tr><td><code>SMEM_BANKS</code></td><td><code>8</code></td><td>Shared Memory</td><td>Number of independent banking domains in local shared SRAM.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <!-- Microarchitectural Deep-Dive -->
        <div class="dossier-deep-dive" style="background: #f8fafc; border-left: 3px solid #3b82f6; padding: 0.85rem 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;">
          <h4 style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 900; color: #1e3a8a; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">Microarchitectural Deep-Dive:</h4>
          <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.5; color: #334155; margin: 0;">Vortex tolerates long memory latencies through dynamic zero-cycle warp interleaving. When warp 0 stalls waiting for an L1 cache miss, the warp scheduler immediately switches execution to warp 1 in the next clock cycle. Control divergence is handled by pushing thread active masks onto a hardware divergence stack.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Verified Benchmarks Table -->
        <h4 style="font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 800; margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #151b20;">&bull; Cycle-Accurate Verified Benchmark Results</h4>
